## The CAPRI → Kill Chain Connection

The CAPRI trial (ceralasertib + olaparib for post-PARPi patients) is the motivation behind CrisPRO's Kill Chain system:

```
Kill Chain monitors:
  CA-125 serial readings (rising = resistance signal)
  HRD shift (declining = HR restoration = PARPi resistance)
  Repair pathway shift (RAD51 activity change)

When 2-of-3 trigger:
  resistance_risk_score drops to 0.20 (HIGH risk)
  System recommends reconsidering PARPi-based therapy
```

The CAPRI trial result is embedded in that logic. "Post-PARPi patients don't respond to ceralasertib+olaparib" → "we need to detect PARPi resistance before recommending olaparib combinations" → "the Kill Chain monitors for exactly the molecular events that drive resistance".

This trial is not just a validation receipt. It's the biological argument for why the Kill Chain needs to exist.

